Each call to [`next`] returns a message if there is one ready to be received. The iterator
never blocks waiting for the next message.

[`next`]: Iterator::next

# Examples

```
use std::thread;
use std::time::Duration;
use crossbeam_channel::unbounded;

let (s, r) = unbounded::<i32>();

thread::spawn(move || {
    s.send(1).unwrap();
