Tries to read bytes from this reader.

Returns the total number of bytes that were read from this reader.

# Examples

```
let (mut r, mut w) = piper::pipe(1024);

// `try_drain()` returns 0 off the bat.
let mut buf = [0; 10];
assert_eq!(r.try_drain(&mut buf), 0);

